    }
   ],
   "html": "<p>We kicked off the night with the film's cast, Director, and a curated list of IHC-invited VIPs on the electric red carpet! Attendees enjoyed pep rally-themed activities including a yearbook photo wall, a decked-out locker room concessions stand, and spirited performances by a cheer squad and drumline.</p>\n<p>DJ Quinn Blake kept the vibes high all night long, while a medium provided readings for guests. Photographer and Y2K icon The Cobrasnake captured the fun party vibes of guests enjoying the scene, making for a festive evening that resulted in an abundance of social content to encourage fans to watch the film!</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Decor",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text2",
     "left": "<p>Transforming the theater into a high school dance was just the foundation. We layered in supernatural elements that tied seamlessly into the film throughout the guest experience. Ouija boards topped the high-top tables, and a graveyard of character tombstones surrounded the medium's reading station.</p>",
     "right": "<p>Decorated lockers and painted signs with chants like “If You Got It Haunt It” were placed as accents to the concessions table. For a final touch, a Darby and the Dead title logo neon sign took center stage as a part of the DJ booth, surrounded by groovy disco ball decor.</p>"
